{"id":"d7cd34c8146c8621","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-zfc-ana-distribution-space.md","title":"ZFC Ana Distribution Space","display":"df-zfc-ana-distribution-space — ZFC Ana Distribution Space","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-ana-distribution-space","aliases":["58-df-zfc-ana-distribution-space","58-df-zfc-analysis2-distribution-space"],"display":"df-zfc-ana-distribution-space — ZFC Ana Distribution Space","depends_on":["[[../batch03/58-df-distribution.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-ana-distribution-space"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-ana-distribution-space</span><span>58-df-zfc-analysis2-distribution-space</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-ana-distribution-space — ZFC Ana Distribution Space"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c53fe47de39217ed\" href=\"?note=c53fe47de39217ed\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-distribution.md\">../batch03/58-df-distribution.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\">\\(E\\)</span> (candidate set of distributions)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal D&#39;(\\Omega)\">\\(\\mathcal D&#39;(\\Omega)\\)</span> (canonical distribution space, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"c53fe47de39217ed\" href=\"?note=c53fe47de39217ed\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-distribution.md\">../batch03/58-df-distribution.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcAnaDistributionSpace}_S(E,\\Omega,n)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcAnaDistributionSpace}_S(E,\\Omega,n)\\)</span> (compatibility predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}ana\\text{-}distribution\\text{-}space} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcAnaDistributionSpace}_S(E,\\Omega,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\land E=\\mathcal D&#39;(\\Omega)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}ana\\text{-}distribution\\text{-}space} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcAnaDistributionSpace}_S(E,\\Omega,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\land E=\\mathcal D&#39;(\\Omega)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This compatibility predicate points to the distribution space already characterized extensionally in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c53fe47de39217ed\" href=\"?note=c53fe47de39217ed\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-distribution.md\">../batch03/58-df-distribution.md</a>; it does not redefine <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal D&#39;(\\Omega)\">\\(\\mathcal D&#39;(\\Omega)\\)</span> through an unparameterized continuity predicate.</li>\n<li><code>58-df-zfc-analysis2-distribution-space</code> remains an alias of this file, not a second predicate.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch03/58-df-distribution.md","status":"resolved","id":"c53fe47de39217ed","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-distribution.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch03/58-df-distribution.md","status":"resolved","id":"c53fe47de39217ed","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathcal D'(\\Omega)$ (canonical distribution space, see [[../batch03/58-df-distribution.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch03/58-df-distribution.md","status":"resolved","id":"c53fe47de39217ed","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Remark]","excerpt":"This compatibility predicate points to the distribution space already characterized extensionally in [[../batch03/58-df-distribution.md]]; it does not redefine $\\mathcal D'(\\Omega)$ through an unparameterized continuity predicate.","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"E","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal D'(\\Omega)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcAnaDistributionSpace}_S(E,\\Omega,n)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}ana\\text{-}distribution\\text{-}space} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcAnaDistributionSpace}_S(E,\\Omega,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\land E=\\mathcal D'(\\Omega)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathcal D'(\\Omega)","display":false}],"bytes":1274,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1437","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-zfc-ana-distribution-space.md|58-df-zfc-ana-distribution-space]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["c53fe47de39217ed"]}